// Carrying: a backpack worn on the back, a basket in a hand, what each can
// bear, and how a load slows a walk (VILLAGE.md decision 11); and handling,
// the goals every topic uses to move a thing to where it goes (METHODS.md).
//
// Cut points:
// - full:     a pack is a container that goes where its carrier goes: a
//             backpack on the back (shouldered: held, but by no hand, so
//             both stay free), a basket in a hand (taken, as anything is).
//             A belted container (#Belted: a pouch, leatherwork/) hangs at
//             the belt likewise: held, by no hand, one at a time, put
//             there from a hand, the ground or a container (`belt_on`).
//             What is put in it is carried with it, and seen only by whoever
//             put it there or looks in. It bears no more than its `load`:
//             what would make it heavier isn't put in. Carried mass (all
//             that is held, hands and back, and what is in it) beyond the
//             `burden`'s `light` slows a walk, by half at `light` and
//             `slows` more. What an operation that stows takes, or is
//             handed (`gather`, `pick_up`; butchering; seed kept back; a
//             purchase), goes into
//             the pack if it fits, else a free hand. Unpacked, a thing is
//             taken out into a free hand (as from any container) and put
//             where it goes. A household's
//             packs are its own, kept by its door: whoever needs one takes
//             it, and puts it back there after, emptied: food, hides,
//             leather and seed into the larder, firewood onto the woodpile. (Seed kept
//             back into a pack worn to market was never emptied, and the
//             pack never put back.) Handling: a thing (`thing`, bound by
//             the topic's way with #Achieve's `with`) taken in hand,
//             unpacked beside where it goes (`into`), or gathered or
//             picked up, a hand freed first by putting down what it
//             carries.
// - reduced:  the same; a walk's pace is set as it starts each tile.
// - abstract: as reduced. A load as a household's capacity to move goods,
//             below reduced, is open (DETAIL_REGIMES.md).
// - frozen:   the same: a pack is a thing.
// - hunger, hunting, farming, firewood: what is emptied where is theirs
//             (#Food, #Hide, #Seed, firewood).
// - market, hunting, firewood: their ways of carrying (market/,
//             hunting/, firewood/) use a pack when the household's is free,
//             and their hands when it isn't; their unpacking, bringing home
//             and freeing a hand are the handling's.
// - code:     the back and the belt are hand slots past the hands (8 and
//             9: BG_BACK, BG_BELT), which take a worn pack and what is
//             belted, and nothing else, one each: the committer's to keep
//             (placement obstacles), as the load is; the slowed walk is
//             work_rate's; stowing is `receiving`. Shouldering, belting,
//             taking into a pack and putting the pack back are declared
//             (actions.tri): moves into a hand that say which.

package carrying

// A pack: a container carried, bearing no more than its `load`; worn on the
// back (`worn`), or held in a hand.
#Pack: #Container & {
    @component(Pack)
    load: mass         @field(content, saved, inspect, perceive(sight))
    worn: *false | true @field(content, saved, inspect, perceive(sight))
}

pack_seen: #Seen & { kindOf: "#Pack" } @family(seen)

backpack: #Pack & { material: "leather", mass: 1kg, capacity: 6, load: 25kg, worn: true }
basket:   #Pack & { material: "wicker", mass: 500g, capacity: 4, load: 8kg }

backpack_look: #Look & { kindOf: "backpack", look: "pack.back" } @family(looks)
basket_look:   #Look & { kindOf: "basket", look: "pack.basket" } @family(looks)

// What a walker carries without slowing (`light`), and how much more halves
// its pace (`slows`): a third at twice that, and so on.
#Burden: { light: mass, slows: mass }

burden: #Burden & { light: 15kg, slows: 40kg } @family(burden)

// Shoulder a backpack: from the ground or a container in reach, onto the
// back (hand 8: no hand is used), if nothing is there already. Two seconds.
shoulder: #Operation & {
    duration: 2s
    roles: {
        actor: #Agent & { id: $a }
        item:  #Pack & { id: $i, worn: true, place: #OnTile | #Inside }
    }
    moves: [#Moves & { moved: $i, into: #Held & { by: $a, hand: 8 } }]
} @family(operations)

// A container worn at the belt: held, by no hand, as a backpack is on the
// back; one at a time.
#Belted: #Container & {}

// Hang something belted at the belt (hand 9: no hand is used): from the
// actor's hand, the ground or a container in reach, if nothing hangs there
// already. Two seconds. It is taken off as anything held is put anywhere.
belt_on: #Operation & {
    duration: 2s
    roles: {
        actor: #Agent & { id: $a }
        item:  #Belted & { id: $i, place: #OnTile | #Inside | #Held & { by: $a } }
    }
    moves: [#Moves & { moved: $i, into: #Held & { by: $a, hand: 9 } }]
} @family(operations)

// Gathering some of a stack, or picking something up: as taking (some) is,
// but into a pack the taker carries, if it fits; else a free hand. Ways
// agency takes, not a menu's: the menu's taking is take and take_some
// (`stowing`, not `operations`).
gather: #Taking & {
    stow:      true
    contest:   "quickness"
    parameter: $n & >=1
    roles: {
        actor: #Agent & { id: $a, freeHands: >=1 }
        item:  #Stack & { id: $i, place: #Inside | #OnTile }
    }
    moves: [#Moves & { moved: $i, portion: $n, into: #Held & { by: $a } }]
} @family(stowing)

pick_up: #Taking & {
    stow:    true
    contest: "quickness"
    roles: {
        actor: #Agent & { id: $a, freeHands: >=1 }
        item:  #Body & { id: $i, place: #Inside | #OnTile }
    }
    moves: [#Moves & { moved: $i, into: #Held & { by: $a } }]
} @family(stowing)

// Put a pack back where the household keeps it: down beside something in
// reach (its larder).
put_back: #Operation & {
    roles: {
        actor:       #Agent & { id: $a }
        item:        #Pack & { id: $i, place: #Held & { by: $a } }
        destination: #Body & { place: $p & #OnTile }
    }
    moves: [#Moves & { moved: $i, into: $p }]
} @family(operations)

// Handling: what every topic that moves a thing to where it goes shares
// (bringing it home, setting it out, putting it away): the thing, `thing`;
// where it goes, `into`; the pack the agent carries; and what it puts down
// to free a hand, `burden`. A topic's frame is a #Handling, so these slots
// pass between its goals and the ones here: its way binds `thing` and
// `into` to what it means (the goods, the household's supply), and the
// ways here do the rest, whatever the thing is.
#Handling: #Frame & { thing: #Body, into: #Body, pack: #Body, burden: #Body }

// Carrying: the pack, where the household keeps it (by its larder,
// `home`), and its woodpile.
#Carrying: #Handling & { home: #Body, woodpile: #Body }

// What may be put down to free a hand: goods (a stack of food, seed or
// firewood), a hide, a log, a tool. Never coins, nor a meal, nor a pack.
let burdens = #Food & #Stack | #Seed & #Stack | #Stack & { unit: "firewood" } | #Hide | #Log | #Axe | #Bow

// A hand free: what it carries put down.
hand_free: #Goal & {
    title: "free a hand"
    done:  { find: [], match: #Handling & { me: #Agent & { freeHands: >=1 } } }
} @family(goals)

put_down_a_burden: #Method & {
    title: "put down what it carries"
    goal:  "hand_free"
    rank:  1
    pre:   { find: ["burden"], match: #Handling & { me: #Agent & { id: $me }, burden: burdens & { place: #Held & { by: $me } } } }
    steps: [#Do & { op: "put_down", object: "burden" }]
} @family(methods)

// Beside where the thing goes (`into`, bound).
beside_into: #Goal & {
    title: "go where it goes"
    done:  #Reached & { reached: "into" }
} @family(goals)

go_there: #Method & {
    title: "go there"
    goal:  "beside_into"
    rank:  1
    pre:   { find: ["into"], match: #Handling & { into: #Body } }
    steps: [#Do & { op: "go_beside", object: "into" }]
} @family(methods)

// Go beside something: what walking there does when it gets there. A way
// agency takes, not a menu's (as `gather` is).
go_beside: #Looking @family(going)

// The thing (`thing`, bound) in a hand, to put where it goes (`into`,
// bound): out of the pack, beside where it goes, so it is carried there
// in the pack; else taken up where it lies, a hand freed first: a stack
// gathered and a thing picked up, into the pack if it fits (it is
// unpacked where it goes), else into the hand.
thing_in_hand: #Goal & {
    title: "take it in hand"
    done:  { find: ["thing"], match: #Handling & { me: #Agent & { id: $me }, thing: #Body & { place: #Held & { by: $me, hand: <8 } } } }
} @family(goals)

unpack_it: #Method & {
    title: "unpack it"
    goal:  "thing_in_hand"
    rank:  1
    pre: {
        find:  ["pack", "thing"]
        match: #Handling & { me: #Agent & { id: $me }, pack: #Pack & { id: $p, place: #Held & { by: $me } },
                             thing: #Body & { place: #Inside & { container: $p } } }
    }
    steps: [#Achieve & { subgoal: "beside_into" }, #Achieve & { subgoal: "hand_free" }, #Do & { op: "take", object: "thing" }]
} @family(methods)

gather_it_up: #Method & {
    title: "gather it up"
    goal:  "thing_in_hand"
    rank:  2
    pre:   { find: ["thing"], match: #Handling & { thing: #Stack & { place: #Inside | #OnTile } } }
    steps: [#Achieve & { subgoal: "hand_free" }, #Do & { op: "gather", object: "thing", units: 10000 }]
} @family(methods)

pick_it_up: #Method & {
    title: "pick it up"
    goal:  "thing_in_hand"
    rank:  3
    pre:   { find: ["thing"], match: #Handling & { thing: #Body & { place: #Inside | #OnTile } } }
    steps: [#Achieve & { subgoal: "hand_free" }, #Do & { op: "pick_up", object: "thing" }]
} @family(methods)

pack_worn: #Goal & {
    title: "take the pack"
    done: {
        find:  ["pack"]
        match: #Carrying & { me: #Agent & { id: $me }, pack: #Pack & { worn: true, place: #Held & { by: $me } } }
    }
} @family(goals)

shoulder_the_pack: #Method & {
    title: "shoulder the pack"
    goal:  "pack_worn"
    rank:  1
    pre:   { find: ["pack"], match: #Carrying & { pack: #Pack & { worn: true, place: #OnTile | #Inside } } }
    order: ["own", "near"]
    steps: [#Do & { op: "shoulder", object: "pack" }]
} @family(methods)

// A pack of any kind, for a buyer: the backpack, else the basket, in hand.
pack_carried: #Goal & {
    title: "take a pack"
    done: {
        find:  ["pack"]
        match: #Carrying & { me: #Agent & { id: $me }, pack: #Pack & { place: #Held & { by: $me } } }
    }
} @family(goals)

shoulder_a_pack: #Method & {
    title: "shoulder the pack"
    goal:  "pack_carried"
    rank:  1
    pre:   { find: ["pack"], match: #Carrying & { pack: #Pack & { worn: true, place: #OnTile | #Inside } } }
    order: ["own", "near"]
    steps: [#Do & { op: "shoulder", object: "pack" }]
} @family(methods)

take_the_basket: #Method & {
    title: "take the basket"
    goal:  "pack_carried"
    rank:  2
    pre:   { find: ["pack"], match: #Carrying & { me: #Agent & { freeHands: >=1 }, pack: #Pack & { worn: false, place: #OnTile | #Inside } } }
    order: ["own", "near"]
    steps: [#Do & { op: "take", object: "pack" }]
} @family(methods)

// The day done: the pack emptied, what is in it put where the household
// keeps it (firewood on the woodpile, anything else in the larder), and
// put back by the larder (`home`; both bound). One whole way: emptied,
// then put back; emptied, each thing in it taken in hand by where it goes
// and put in.
pack_returned: #Goal & {
    title: "put the pack back"
    done:  #Did & { did: "put_back" }
} @family(goals)

return_it: #Method & {
    title: "put it back"
    goal:  "pack_returned"
    rank:  1
    pre:   { find: ["pack"], match: #Carrying & { me: #Agent & { id: $me }, pack: #Pack & { place: #Held & { by: $me } } } }
    steps: [#Achieve & { subgoal: "pack_emptied" }, #Do & { op: "put_back", object: "pack", target: "home" }]
} @family(methods)

// Emptied: nothing it believes is in the pack (bound), nor anything kept
// at home in its hands (what it took out of the pack, and goods carried):
// firewood onto the woodpile; food, seed, hides and leather (a piece
// bought, short of a lot: market/), and anything else out of the pack,
// into the larder. Food kept is raw, a stack or a portion
// bought on its own; a meal carried to eat isn't.
let kept   = #Food & { raw: true } | #Food & #Stack | #Seed & #Stack | #Hide | #Leather
let wood   = #Stack & { unit: "firewood" }
let packed = #Carrying & { pack: #Pack & { id: $p }, thing: #Body & { place: #Inside & { container: $p } } }
let held   = #Carrying & { me: #Agent & { id: $me }, thing: (kept | wood) & { place: #Held & { by: $me, hand: <8 } } }

pack_emptied: #Goal & {
    title: "empty the pack"
    done:  #None & { find: ["pack", "thing"], match: packed | held }
} @family(goals)

onto_the_woodpile: #Method & {
    title: "stack it on the woodpile"
    goal:  "pack_emptied"
    rank:  1
    pre:   { find: ["pack", "thing"], match: packed & { thing: wood } | held & { thing: wood } }
    steps: [#Achieve & { subgoal: "thing_in_hand", with: [{ binds: "into", to: "woodpile" }] },
            #Do & { op: "put_in", object: "thing", target: "woodpile" }]
} @family(methods)

into_the_larder: #Method & {
    title: "put it in the larder"
    goal:  "pack_emptied"
    rank:  2
    pre:   { find: ["pack", "thing"], match: packed | held }
    steps: [#Achieve & { subgoal: "thing_in_hand", with: [{ binds: "into", to: "home" }] },
            #Do & { op: "put_in", object: "thing", target: "home" }]
} @family(methods)
